    "updated_at": "2022-12-07T08:04:16Z",
    "body": "@a4sriniv updated his tests and confirm that everyone matches Chrome's behavior. So, I put up a PR in https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/8587 to fix that. I think we should just merge that, and if we want to reconsider changing to better behavior in the future, we can do that separately.\r\n\r\nI investigated theme-color, color-scheme, and supports-reduced-motion for Chromium ([source](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/blink/renderer/core/html/html_meta_element.cc)), and they all work in the more-reasonable way the current spec suggests. `viewport`, `handheldfriendly`, and `mobileoptimized` appear to use `referrer`-like weird behavior, but they are not really standardized...",
